title: Microsoft Entra Cloud Sync: Synchronized objects
agents: special_entra_cloudsync
catalog: cloud/azure
license: GPLv2
distribution: checkmk-entra-cloudsync
description:
 Reports the synchronized object counts published by the Cloud Sync synchronization job.
 <br>
 Data source: Microsoft Graph v1.0, GET /servicePrincipals/[service-principal-id]/synchronization/jobs/[job-id].
 <br>
 Monitored field: status.synchronizedEntryCountByType.
 <br>
 Service output: each returned object-type mapping is shown as "type: count", for example "user to User: 3". The count is the number of synchronized entries for that mapping; it is not an error count. A metric is created for each returned mapping.
 <br>
 State mapping: this service is informational and remains OK when counts are present or when Microsoft reports no object counts. Missing job data is UNKNOWN.
 <br>
 Vendor documentation: https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/graph/api/resources/synchronization-synchronizationstatus?view=graph-rest-1.0
item:
 The Microsoft Entra Cloud Sync configuration name, derived from the Cloud Sync service principal display name. The synchronization job ID is used as a fallback if no display name is available.
discovery:
 One service is discovered for each synchronization job returned for the configured service principal whose templateId is AD2AADProvisioning.
